      "hints": [
        "Isolate $x$ in $y = \\frac{2}{3 - 2x}$ to get $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{x}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = \\frac{2}{3 - 2x}$ and rearrange to solve for $x$:\n$$y(3 - 2x) = 2 \\implies 3 - 2x = \\frac{2}{y}$$\n$$2x = 3 - \\frac{2}{y} \\implies x = \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{y}$$",
        "Write the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{x} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } \\frac{3x - 2}{2x}\\right)$$"
