      "hints": [
        "Find $g^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - a}{4}$.",
        "Equate $\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{x - a}{4} \\implies x^2 - (a + 6)x + 4 = 0$.",
        "Set discriminant $(a + 6)^2 - 16 = 0 \\implies a = -2$ or $a = -10$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the inverse function $g^{-1}(x)$:\n$$y = 4x + a \\implies x = \\frac{y - a}{4} \\implies g^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - a}{4}$$",
        "Equate $f^{-1}(x) = g^{-1}(x)$:\n$$\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{x - a}{4}$$",
        "Multiply through by $4x$ and rearrange into standard quadratic form:\n$$6x - 4 = x(x - a) = x^2 - ax \\implies x^2 - (a + 6)x + 4 = 0$$",
        "For the equation to have two equal real roots, set the discriminant equal to zero:\n$$\\Delta = [-(a + 6)]^2 - 4(1)(4) = 0$$\n$$(a + 6)^2 - 16 = 0 \\implies (a + 6)^2 = 16$$\n$$a + 6 = \\pm 4 \\implies a = -6 \\pm 4$$\n$$a = -2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = -10$$"
      ],
